Z||000000||dodger||05-01-2000||10:02 PM||||So there I was getting gas last Tuesday morning when my 86SE 2.8 quit. Well the short version of the story is I called the Fiero Shop right away, then had AAA tow it the 70 miles there. Well, by early evening George had replaced the fuel pump. Since George knows my Fiero is my only transport he volunteered to drive down 70 miles and pick me up! Which he did...and then let me drive his 88GT back, over HWY 17, which for you that live elsewhere is a 4 lane mountain racetrack. Where else in this world can you break down in the morning, have it fixed the same day, be picked up 70 miles away, and drive the boss's 88GT to pick up your car, and drive your car home that night!? Amazing...<BR>Thanks George!!!<P>Plus...now I know the difference in performance and what mods to make to my 86SE...      ||||reg||10
Z||000001||stimpy||05-02-2000||07:42 AM||||What did I tell ya, is George the MAN or WHAT? Is there no limit to this mans kindness and generosity? And the capper is that you prob paid -20% then you would have at Goodwremch!. <P>Oh to drive 17 in my Fiero! Without the traffic of course!||||reg||1
